# dotfiles repo for $HOME — paired with `git config status.showUntrackedFiles normal`
# (user decision 2026-09-02; it was `no` before that).
#
# Strategy:
#   - Untracked files at $HOME root (caches, creds, IDE state, language toolchains,
#     nested project repos, app state) stay visible as untracked under
#     showUntrackedFiles=normal; they are NOT covered by ignore rules. Don't
#     re-add a $HOME-root deny list here — the deny list was unmaintainable
#     (every new app dropped a new untracked dir we had to chase).
#   - This file's job is now narrower: keep `git add <dir>` safe for the deny
#     region (.config/) and the deny-then-whitelist regions (.local/, .gemini/),
#     and pattern-block build artefacts inside tracked subtrees.
#   - `git status` collapses untracked directories; `git status -uall` expands the
#     whole tree and is slow (see CLAUDE.md → Repo shape for the numbers).
#   - .ssh/ and other cred dirs are not in this file. They stay untracked and
#     visible; if you ever `git add` one explicitly, that's a deliberate decision
#     and you should split secrets out first
#     (see CLAUDE.md → Repo shape, the .ssh/ bullet).
#
# When adding a new tracked file:
#   - At $HOME root: just `git add <path>`. It shows as `??` in `git status`
#     until you add it.
#   - Under .local/, .gemini/: add a `!`-rule per level, same pattern as before
#     (`!/.local/foo/`, `!/.local/foo/**`). Open every directory level.

# editor / shell backups (apply repo-wide so they don't sneak into tracked subtrees)
*~
*.swp
*.swo
\#*\#
.\#*

# build artefacts inside any tracked subtree
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# ============================================================
# .config/: ~/.config is itself one independent git repo
# (remote in GITS.org). Since 2026-09-03 it owns the whole
# tracked .config tree — the six per-app clones that used to
# sit inside it are ordinary directories of that repo now.
# It is NOT tracked by the parent dotfiles repo; it shows up as
# `?? .config/` under status.showUntrackedFiles=normal. The deny
# rule below prevents an accidental `git add .config/` here from
# sweeping in app state. Its own ignore rules live inside that
# repo, in per-directory .gitignore files — don't mirror them here.
# ============================================================
/.config/*

# ============================================================
# .local/: deny-then-whitelist
# ============================================================
/.local/*
!/.local/bin/
/.local/bin/*
!/.local/bin/claude-editor
!/.local/bin/claude-editor-gui
!/.local/bin/mqpub
!/.local/bin/mqsend
!/.local/bin/mqstop
!/.local/bin/zoxide-seed.sh
# fcitx5-rime user config (schema selection). build/, *.userdb/, installation.yaml stay ignored.
!/.local/share/
/.local/share/*
!/.local/share/fcitx5/
/.local/share/fcitx5/*
!/.local/share/fcitx5/rime/
/.local/share/fcitx5/rime/*
!/.local/share/fcitx5/rime/*.custom.yaml

# ============================================================
# .gemini/: cred-bearing app dir — strict whitelist, NEVER use **
# ============================================================
# Contains oauth_creds.json, google_accounts.json, installation_id, history/,
# mailbox/. Whitelist files one by one.
/.gemini/*
!/.gemini/settings.json
!/.gemini/bin/
/.gemini/bin/*
!/.gemini/bin/talk_claude.sh
!/.gemini/skills/
!/.gemini/skills/**
